    <owl:Ontology>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql"/>
        <terms:created xml:lang="en">2017-10-22</terms:created>
        <terms:description xml:lang="en">This ontology describes the spatial features of things used in a smart environment. Thease feartures include the geometerical representation of objects along with the spatial and directional relations between them. This ontology relies on the two other spatial related ontologies http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql and http://www.observedchange.com/tisc/ns/</terms:description>
        <terms:title xml:lang="en">Smart Environment Geometry Ontology Pattern</terms:title>
        <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix xml:lang="en">se-geometry</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
        <vann:preferredNamespaceUri rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/smartenvironment/patterns/geometry.owl"/>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements xml:lang="en">What are the spatial relations among objects or sections in a smart environment?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf rdf:resource="http://www.observedchange.com/tisc/ns"/>
        <cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf rdf:resource="http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x37; term declared x2;
- file: pattern.owl declares &lt;http://purl.org/dc/terms/created&gt; as an annotation property, as pattern.ttl did
- file: pattern.owl declares &lt;http://purl.org/dc/terms/description&gt; as an annotation property, as pattern.ttl did
- file: pattern.owl declares &lt;http://purl.org/dc/terms/title&gt; as an annotation property, as pattern.ttl did
- file: pattern.owl declares &lt;http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#coversRequirements&gt; as an annotation property, as pattern.ttl did
- file: pattern.owl declares &lt;http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#isSpecializationOf&gt; as an annotation property, as pattern.ttl did
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.observedchange.com/tisc/ns/"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql"/>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


